course: dictionary
lesson: 13198
title: Fulfilment: a feeling and a finished promise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fulfilment comes from the verb fulfil, which means to carry out or complete something. The ending -ment turns it into a noun, a name for a feeling or a thing. When you meet a new noun, ask: is this a thing, a feeling, or an action? Then read the words around it for clues.
explain: «Mia felt a deep sense of fulfilment after painting the mural.» The words sense of and felt tell you this is a feeling. Mia was happy and satisfied because she had made something worthwhile. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Mia felt a deep sense of being happy and satisfied." It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: «The fulfilment of Sam's dream came when he scored in the final.» Here fulfilment means that the dream came true. The word of links it to the dream, so the clue is that something hoped for has now happened. Fulfilment can also mean packing and sending out orders, as in «an order fulfilment centre», so always check the sentence.
fact: Fulfilment is a noun. It names a feeling or a thing.
fact: Fulfilment means a happy, satisfied feeling from doing something useful or something you love.
fact: Fulfilment also means doing what was promised, hoped or needed, as in «the fulfilment of a promise».
fact: In business, fulfilment means packing and sending out orders, as in «an order fulfilment centre».
fact: Fulfilment is UK spelling. In the US it is spelled «fulfillment», with two l's.
exercise: «Mia felt a deep sense of fulfilment after painting the mural.» What does fulfilment mean here? | Packing parcels in a shop | Being bored and tired | *A happy feeling of having done something worthwhile | Lost property
exercise: «The fulfilment of Sam's dream came when he scored in the final.» What does fulfilment mean here? | *The dream came true | A new football kit | Sam was sleeping | A dream was forgotten
exercise: «The shop has a big order fulfilment centre.» What does a fulfilment centre do? | Teaches children to swim | Cooks lunch for schools | Sells old furniture | *Packs and sends out orders
test: «Grandma felt fulfilment when she taught her grandchildren to read.» What feeling does this sentence show? | Boredom | Hunger | Anger | *Happiness and satisfaction
test: Fulfilment is which part of speech? | *Noun | Verb | Adverb | Adjective
exam: «Ella promised to finish her project, and the fulfilment of that promise made her proud.» What does fulfilment of that promise mean? | Breaking the promise | Forgetting the promise | Writing the promise down | *Keeping the promise by doing what was promised
